  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-IP24-TLS128</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved labour regulations and compliance, Occupational Safety and Health, elimination of child labour and protection of women&apos;s rights</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Based on the 2022 Housing Census, 24,122 children aged 10&#x2013;17 were engaged in work, accounting for 10 per cent of the total child population in that age group. This highlights the urgent need to strengthen the legal and institutional framework in Timor-Leste to eliminate child labour and ensure safe, decent, and violence-free working conditions for all.
In response, the ILO continues its collaboration with the Government of Timor-Leste to strengthen national efforts in eliminating child labour and promoting safe and decent work for all. This includes supporting the approval of the National Action Plan for the Elimination of Child Labour, finalizing the list of hazardous work prohibited for children, and integrating the reporting and referral mechanisms into official labour inspection guidelines. The ILO also continues to provide technical assistance for the finalization and submission of the draft law on the elimination of violence and harassment in the world of work. These initiatives are expected to lead to stronger enforcement of labour protections, reduced incidence of child labour, and improved workplace safety and dignity for all workers in Timor-Leste.</narrative>
  </description>
